Expected elements: present

Identity bar: truncated hash, `Succeeded`, `block 63675`, both stepping directions grouped, `128 / 345`, the named phase rail, and an exit to `aztec-testnet`. Provenance is the first row of the Transaction pane — `DATA`, an affirmative `Real Aztec testnet data` badge toned like `Succeeded` and `Trace ready`, then the capture's endpoint, moment and replay window. No band above the identity bar. Code, Call Trace and Values each explain the absent symbols in their own words; `Supply sources` present. No invented source, no fixture content, no engine banner.

The copy is the strongest thing here. All three panes put the limitation on the chain, not on the product — bytecode without debug symbols — and none of them apologises or renders as an error. The band's removal is a clear register win: the shell is now identity bar plus panes, exactly the desktop vocabulary, with no full-width interruption. What it did not fix is the pane interiors. The explanations are set as web-register paragraphs at a ~590px measure, top-left of otherwise empty panes, with no empty-state treatment; the shell reads as the tool and the pane contents read as a document dropped into it.

Highest-priority fixes: give the source-starved panes a designed empty state in the desktop idiom rather than free prose; rename `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` from the product vocabulary, not the adapter field.

Rating: 6/10

